From c02d3a2b1b941df135b5cca7afc5b1bfc0da2024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:43:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02263/11362] [outer-loop] GPU-enforce LocalGGUFProposer via
 CUDA llama.cpp binary (always-GPU directive)

Operator directive 2026-06-17: open-weight SOTA models must ALWAYS load on GPU; CPU is
excruciatingly slow + pegs ~20 cores (fights the conductor). Root cause: the venv
llama-cpp-python is CPU-only (llama_supports_gpu_offload()==False), so n_gpu_layers=-1
silently fell back to CPU (the 22-core gemma hog). Fix: LocalGGUFProposer now invokes the
CUDA-built llama.cpp binary (~/.cache/llama.cpp-master/build/bin/llama-cli -ngl 999),
confirmed offloading gemma-4-12B across the 2x3090s (~14GB VRAM, ~1 CPU core). GPU-ENFORCED:
fails LOUD if the binary is missing -- no silent CPU fallback. Unblocks fast local
induction (no codex contention; the codex refactor round just timed out at 600s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
